<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Celtici</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 138 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic communities of south-western Iberia, said by Pliny to have migrated from Celtiberia, living in the Alentejo and western Andalusia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> and Pliny describe Celtici in the south-west, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> and the Atlantic and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beturia">Beturia</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/extremadura">Extremadura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huelva">Huelva</a>. Pliny says they came from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/celtiberians">Celtiberians</a>, as shown by their religion, language and town names, though the date of their arrival is uncertain, probably from the 5th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in fortified settlements such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nertobriga-beturia">Nertobriga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirobriga">Mirobriga</a>, whose -briga names are Celtic. Their society of farmers and herders lay close to the mining districts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-morena">Sierra Morena</a>. They seem to have been a group of communities rather than a single polity.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Their territory was drawn into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a> and was pacified after the Lusitanian wars and the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decimus-junius-brutus-callaicus">Decimus Junius Brutus</a> from 138 BCE. Under Augustus it was split between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lusitania">Lusitania</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-baetica">Baetica</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/celtici.jpg" alt="Celtici" width="320" height="298"><figcaption>Image: The Ogre · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethnographic_Iberia_200_BCE.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 138 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a>, <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Celts of the south-west</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-319&amp;focus=celtici" aria-label="Celtici on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4476 759 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Celtici lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1072h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4796 1015h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4796 1015h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Portugal. <a href="/atlas?year=-319&amp;focus=celtici">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
